<title>INDIA: Indian repo auction cut-off steady at 5.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Indian repo auction cut-off steady at 5.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Monday it maintained the cut-off at 5.0 percent at its four-day repo auction of government securities.</p>
<p>The RBI said it received five bids for 10 billion rupees of which it accepted four for 9.75 billion.</p>
<p>The weighted-average cut-off worked out to 4.9641 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
